cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This branch is an unreleased journal candidate. Cite the published version
  1.1.1 base archive for current reuse and replace this development metadata
  with the final immutable release DOI before citing the candidate additions.
title: >-
  SuRT-Virtual Rwanda: auditable district-scale Earth-data harmonization and
  provenance-labelling reproducibility artifact
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tuyishime
    given-names: Audre Prince
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-0799-3140"
abstract: >-
  Unreleased companion software candidate for an Earth Science Informatics
  Software article. It prepares CHIRPS rainfall, ERA5-Land temperature, MODIS
  vegetation greenness, and HAND terrain descriptors for Rwanda's 30 districts;
  applies a fail-closed provenance and evidence-class contract; and includes
  positive, negative, portability, release-contract, integrity, and scoped
  public-data numerical validation. The candidate extends the published
  version 1.1.1 base archive, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21677162. It is descriptive,
  non-operational, and contains no patient, surveillance, or confidential
  operational data.
version: 1.2.0-dev
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PrinceAudre/surt-virtual-rwanda-repro"
url: "https://github.com/PrinceAudre/surt-virtual-rwanda-repro/tree/codex/earth-science-informatics-refinement-v1.3.0"
keywords:
  - Earth science informatics
  - reproducible research
  - environmental data
  - geospatial workflow
  - data provenance
  - zonal statistics
  - R
